column13:
mfitzp (2023-06-26T09:38:28Z): Having experimented a bit further, this behavior also affects code blocks.  | RohitLakh (2023-06-28T06:06:09Z): @mfitzp It would be helpful if you can specify if you are using the `beta editor` or the `old editor`. | SamarthBagga (2023-06-28T14:54:29Z): Hi @RohitLakh are you working on this issue? | RohitLakh (2023-06-28T15:04:57Z): @SamarthBagga You can pick it up if you want to | SamarthBagga (2023-06-28T15:05:30Z): @RohitLakh thank you ill start working on it.
 | SamarthBagga (2023-06-29T19:17:21Z): It seems like there is no code to handle the undo behavior in the editor, thus it relies on the browser's native undo functionality. I am thinking of adding a custom undo function handler specifically for the callout and code blocks. Is this an acceptable fix ? | mfitzp (2023-07-01T20:33:17Z): @RohitLakh this is on the old editor. I'd just set up on Ghost Pro so wasn't aware there were two options. 

@SamarthBagga Having tried it just now, I can't reproduce this in the beta editor.  | 9larsons (2023-08-29T17:45:51Z): We don't have much appetite to resolve this given we're working hard to move the beta editor out of beta. 

@SamarthBagga if you would like to submit a PR, I can take a look. However if you're just looking to contribute in some fashion - not specifically this issue - I'd recommend checking out another given that we're actively working to phase out mobiledoc. | markstos (2023-09-15T13:38:06Z): I recommend closing this as wont-fix, given that there's a reasonable workaround of switching to the new editor.
